at least one person is dead dozens more  injured after a las vegas-based tour bus  crashed in the state of arizona now we  told you this happened about noon as the  bus was  in route to grand canyon west orco mano  went right to the scene of the crash  tonight  has much more on what we know about the  victims  authorities say the deadly tour bus  crash happened here on this stretch of  diamond bar road  as the bus was headed toward grand  canyon west this  mile marker sign ripped from the ground  this is a photo showing the aftermath of  the crash according to the mohave county  sheriff's office  the tour bus which is managed by a las  vegas-based company  was carrying at least 48 people  including the driver  when it rolled over and landed on its  side one person died at the scene and  two others were critically injured  kingman regional medical center tells us  a total of 44 people were brought to  their facility  two were treated and transported  elsewhere three had serious injuries and  the rest sustained minor injuries  the identities of those involved have  not been released yet  the mojave county sheriff's office says  the investigation into what happened  is still ongoing so stay with us for  updates reporting in medview arizona  orca mana 8 news now
 

